  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the number of outcomes above the average outcome — is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses only on the probability of winning (33% vs. 34%), not on comparing outcomes to the unweighted average (1250 vs. 1200). The decision reason's rule (preferring the lottery with more outcomes above the average) is not applied or referenced in the justification. Since both lotteries have exactly one outcome above the average, the reason would be indifferent, but the individual did not consider this metric. Instead, they used a different criterion (probability of winning). Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the decision process.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
